1
00:00:00,690 --> 00:00:04,230
Welcome to Radiation Safety Basics.
欢迎学习辐射安全基础。

2
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:09,630
The purpose of this video is to explore the sources of radiation, dosimetry, and the basic
本视频的目的是探讨辐射的来源、剂量学，以及

3
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:12,070
biologic effects of radiation.
辐射的基本生物学效应。

4
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:14,190
So let's get started.
那我们开始吧。

5
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:19,750
There are two basic sources of radiation, natural sources that include cosmic, where
辐射有两大基本来源：天然来源，包括宇宙辐射、

6
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:23,870
we get our food, water, or our air, and the ground.
我们从食物、水或空气中摄入的辐射，以及来自地面的辐射。

7
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:28,710
Man-made radiation comes from the nuclear industry and the ionizing radiation we use
人工辐射来自核工业，以及我们在

8
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:30,390
in medical imaging.
医学成像中使用的电离辐射。

9
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:34,030
Let's take a quick look at the annual dose limits.
我们来快速看一下年剂量限值。

10
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:40,150
The general public is limited to 1 millisievert for continuous exposure and 5 millisieverts
公众在持续照射下的限值为 1 毫希沃特，而在不经常的照射下

11
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:42,150
for infrequent exposure.
为 5 毫希沃特。

12
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:46,670
Operators are limited to 50 millisievert or 5 rem a year.
操作人员的限值是每年 50 毫希沃特，即 5 雷姆。

13
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:51,370
Let's look at some basic dosimetry measurements.
我们来看一些基本的剂量学测量单位。

14
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:54,930
A red or a gray refers to an absorbed dose.
拉德（rad）或戈瑞（gray）指的是吸收剂量。

15
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:58,010
Red in fact stands for radiation-absorbed dose.
rad 实际上代表“辐射吸收剂量”（radiation absorbed dose）。

16
00:00:58,010 --> 00:01:01,930
A rem or sievert refers to the unit of dose equivalent.
雷姆或希沃特指的是剂量当量的单位。

17
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:07,690
Rem stands for radiation-equivalent man and is an expression of the biologic response
rem 代表“人体伦琴当量”（radiation equivalent man），它表示的是人体对

18
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:09,850
to radiation.
辐射的生物学反应。

19
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:14,010
Let's look at some basic biologic effects of radiation.
我们来看看辐射的一些基本生物学效应。

20
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:17,310
The human response to radiation is dose-dependent.
人体对辐射的反应取决于剂量。

21
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:20,410
Some cells are more radio-sensitive than others.
有些细胞比其他细胞对辐射更敏感。

22
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:24,930
Response can be categorized as early effects, effects that are seen in a short time after
反应可以分为早期效应，即照射后短时间内

23
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:29,210
the exposure, and late effects that may take years to develop.
出现的效应，以及可能要过好几年才会出现的晚期效应。

24
00:01:29,210 --> 00:01:35,630
The laws of Burgonnay and Tribe and Do state high proliferation rate for cells and a high
Bergonié 和 Tribondeau 定律指出，细胞增殖率高、

25
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:40,670
growth rate for tissues result in an increased radio-sensitivity.
组织生长率高，会导致辐射敏感性增加。

26
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:45,050
This is why we shield gonads when it is all possible and try not to x-ray during
这就是为什么只要有可能我们都会屏蔽性腺，并尽量避免在

27
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:47,650
the first trimester of pregnancy.
怀孕头三个月做 X 射线检查。

28
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:54,530
The early effects of radiation include acute radiation syndrome, local tissue damage, hematologic
辐射的早期效应包括急性放射综合征、局部组织损伤、造血

29
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:57,450
depression, and cytogenic damage.
抑制以及细胞遗传学损伤。

30
00:01:57,450 --> 00:02:02,310
An early response occurs within minutes or days after radiation exposure.
早期反应发生在受照后几分钟到几天内。

31
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:07,250
When performed properly, these effects are never seen in general x-ray.
如果操作得当，这些效应在普通 X 射线检查中是绝不会出现的。

32
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:11,310
Late effects of radiation happen months or years after exposure.
辐射的晚期效应发生在受照后几个月或几年。

33
00:02:11,310 --> 00:02:17,090
Both early and late effects need a high dose of radiation to occur, but we should be always
早期和晚期效应都需要高剂量辐射才会发生，但我们应该始终

34
00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:26,040
ever cautious and assume even small doses are harmful, since dose is cumulative.
保持谨慎，假定即使是小剂量也是有害的，因为剂量是会累积的。

35
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:30,480
There are many examples of local tissue damage by radiation.
辐射造成局部组织损伤的例子有很多。

36
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:33,420
The first is erythema, or skin reddening.
第一个是红斑，也就是皮肤发红。

37
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:40,920
This response is followed by desquamicization, which is a form of skin ulceration.
这种反应之后会出现脱皮，这是皮肤溃疡的一种形式。

38
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:44,400
The gonads are affected, in particular the sperm in the ooze sites, and these are the
性腺会受到影响，尤其是精子和卵母细胞，它们是

39
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:51,720
most radio-sensitive cells while they are in the stem cells phase.
处于干细胞阶段时对辐射最敏感的细胞。

40
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:59,240
Key biologic factors that affect radio-sensitivity include the oxygen effect, age, recovery,
影响辐射敏感性的关键生物学因素包括氧效应、年龄、恢复

41
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:01,080
and chemical agents.
以及化学制剂。

42
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:06,640
The oxygen effect says tissues are more sensitive to radiation in oxygen.
氧效应是指，组织在有氧条件下对辐射更敏感。

43
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:12,440
Diagnostic x-ray imaging is performed under full oxygenization conditions.
诊断 X 射线成像是在充分氧合的条件下进行的。

44
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:17,000
The age of the biologic structures affect the radio-sensitivity as well, with newest
生物结构的年龄也会影响辐射敏感性，最新的、

45
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,320
youngest being most radio-sensitive.
最年轻的结构对辐射最敏感。

46
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:25,720
History demonstrates cells can recover from radiation damage if the dose is not sufficient
历史表明，如果剂量一开始就不足以杀死细胞，

47
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:28,040
enough to kill the cell in the first place.
细胞是能够从辐射损伤中恢复的。

48
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:32,280
And there are some chemicals that can modify radiation response.
还有一些化学物质可以改变辐射反应。

49
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:36,560
Radioprotector chemicals are not used in humans, unfortunately, because their increased dose
遗憾的是，辐射防护剂不用于人体，因为加大剂量

50
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:40,010
tends to kill the host.
往往会杀死宿主。

51
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:46,090
When looking at dose-response relationships, a linear dose-response relationship is directly
在看剂量—反应关系时，线性剂量—反应关系在画到图上时

52
00:03:46,090 --> 00:03:52,670
proportional to the dose-response when you put it on a graph and can have a threshold
与剂量—反应成正比，它可以有阈值，

53
00:03:52,670 --> 00:03:54,330
or not.
也可以没有。

54
00:03:54,330 --> 00:04:03,490
A threshold-response will occur at some specified value on the chart that is greater than zero.
阈值反应会在图上某个大于零的特定值处出现。

55
00:04:03,490 --> 00:04:11,370
A non-threshold response will occur at any point, regardless of the size of the dose.
无阈值反应则在任何一点都会出现，无论剂量大小。

56
00:04:11,370 --> 00:04:18,790
Linear responses are not directly proportional, and they create a curved line on the chart.
线性反应不是成正比的，它们在图上形成一条曲线。

57
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:23,730
So just remember, a linear will cause a straight line on your charts, non-linear will cause
所以只要记住，线性的在图上是一条直线，非线性的则是

58
00:04:23,730 --> 00:04:26,950
a curved line.
一条曲线。

59
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:32,530
Because the human body is an aqueous solution containing about 80% water, a radiation of
由于人体是一种含有约 80% 水的水溶液，水受到照射

60
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:37,450
water is the principal radiation interaction in the body.
是体内最主要的辐射相互作用。

61
00:04:37,450 --> 00:04:42,370
When water is irradiated, it disassociates into other molecular products.
水受到照射时，会分解成其他分子产物。

62
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:45,990
This is called the radiolisis of water.
这叫做水的辐射分解。

63
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:48,590
Let's look at direct and indirect effects.
我们来看看直接效应和间接效应。

64
00:04:48,590 --> 00:04:54,350
If the initial ionizing event occurs on the target molecule, like a DNA, it is a direct
如果最初的电离事件发生在靶分子上，比如 DNA，那就是直接

65
00:04:54,350 --> 00:04:55,350
effect.
效应。

66
00:04:55,350 --> 00:04:57,930
DNA is a critical target.
DNA 是一个关键靶点。

67
00:04:57,930 --> 00:05:03,990
If it occurs on a distant non-critical molecule, it is an indirect effect.
如果它发生在远处的非关键分子上，那就是间接效应。

68
00:05:03,990 --> 00:05:09,390
The principal effect on humans is indirect, as in radiolisis.
对人体的主要效应是间接效应，比如辐射分解。

69
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:12,810
Low chronic irradiation does not impair fertility.
低剂量的慢性照射不会损害生育能力。

70
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:18,250
All observations point to the first trimester as the most radiosensitive period, in particular
所有观察结果都表明，怀孕头三个月是对辐射最敏感的时期，尤其是

71
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,250
the first two weeks.
头两周。

72
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:26,770
During the period of major organ formation, during weeks 2-10, two effects can occur, skeletal
在主要器官形成期，也就是第 2 到 10 周，可能出现两种效应：骨骼

73
00:05:26,770 --> 00:05:29,090
and organ abnormalities.
异常和器官异常。

74
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:37,480
And the relative risk of leukemia is a risk of 1.5, which is small.
白血病的相对风险是 1.5，这个风险很小。

75
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:41,280
Genetic effects are linear and non-threshold.
遗传效应是线性、无阈值的。

76
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,100
Any dose has risk.
任何剂量都有风险。

77
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:48,440
Frequency of radiation induced is low.
辐射诱发的频率很低。

78
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:51,200
In late effects, we have latent periods.
晚期效应有潜伏期。

79
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:58,400
These include cataracts with a latent period of 5-30 years, leukemia of 4-7 years, and
其中包括白内障，潜伏期为 5 到 30 年；白血病为 4 到 7 年，而且

80
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:04,480
they're still at risk after 20 years, thyroid cancer for about 20 years.
20 年后仍有风险；甲状腺癌大约为 20 年。

81
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:10,180
There are only 8 cases per 10,000 people irradiated with one rad of radiation for
每 10,000 名受到 1 拉德辐射照射的人中，

82
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:15,060
total cases of risk of malignancy.
恶性肿瘤风险的总病例只有 8 例。

83
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:18,580
I want to thank you all for joining me.
感谢大家和我一起学习。

84
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:19,680
Come back, read your book.
回去好好读读你们的课本。

85
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:26,040
A lot of this information came directly from Bichon, so good luck to you, and good luck
这里的很多信息直接来自 Bushong 的书，所以祝你们好运，祝你们

86
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:26,940
on that test.
考试顺利。
